oses.</p><p>The user can deactivate them directly on the Google website.</p><ul><li>Official information on Google's third party cookies (<a href=\\\\\\\"https://business.safety.google/adscookies\\\\\\\" target=\\\\\\\"_blank\\\\\\\">https://business.safety.google/adscookies</a>).</li><li>Google Policy (<a href=\\\\\\\"https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl-pt-BR\\\\\\\" target=\\\\\\\"_blank\\\\\\\">https://policies.google .com/technologies/partner-sites?hl-pt-BR</a>).</li></ul><p>Google Analytics on the gov.br portal has advertising reporting features enabled, which collects information per DoubleClick cookie, such as web activity and device advertising IDs (application activity)(<a href=\\\\\\\"https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/2799357\\\\\\\" target=\\\\\\\" _blank\\\\\\\">https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/2799357</a>)</p><p>The gov.br portal has no control over which third-party cookies will be activated.</p><p>Some third-party cookies that may be found when accessing the portal:</p><p>Domains: Google, Youtube, DoubleClick.net</p>\\\", \\\"groupId\\\": \\\"cookies-de-terceiros\\\"}], \\\"purposeLabel\\\": \\\"Goal\\\", \\\"expiresLabel\\\": \\\"Due date\\\", \\\"cookieGroupsLabel\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"lastUpdate\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"optOutButton\\\": \\\"Manage cookies\\\", \\\"mainTitle\\\": \\\"Advanced cookie settings\\\", \\\"domainLabel\\\": \\\"Domain\\\", \\\"enterpriseLabel\\\": \\\"Company\\\", \\\"onLabel\\\": \\\"On\\\", \\\"lang\\\": \\\"en\\\", \\\"infoText\\\": \\\"To improve your experience on the platform and provide personalized services, we use cookies. <strong>By accepting, you will be able to use all the site's functionalities. By selecting \\\\\\\"Reject Cookies\\\\\\\", those that are not strictly necessary will be disabled</strong>. To choose which ones you want to authorize, select \\\\\\\"Manage Cookies\\\\\\\". Learn more in our <a href=\\\\\\\"https://www.gov.br/pt-br/termos-de-uso\\\\\\\" target=\\\\